{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1140929-the-missing-sea-lion","id":1140929,"title":"The missing Sea Lion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-16T17:03:05-07:00","id":1140929,"title":"The missing Sea Lion","content":"Does anybody knows where are the statistics of a Seal or Sea Lion? Or any animal, for that matter?<br /> <br /> Asking because if is there a Selkie in the Game those statistics would be needed. The Phooka I know that they can be any Animal, so there is never a list big enough to have all of them, but still some basic animals would help.<br /> <br /> Does anyone know where I could find them?<br /> <br /> Thank you all in advance.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T14:03:50-07:00","id":1141887,"title":"","content":"There are Sea Lion stats in Blood-Dimmed Tides. Other than adding a Bite attack they are pretty much the same as a mortal human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15685-up-to-eleven","name":"Up-to-Eleven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T06:00:04-07:00","id":1142112,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the help.<br /> <br /> I looked it up and, yeah, only the most physically inept and unharmed Selkie would gain much of an advantage becoming an Sea Lion in battle. Maybe if it is going on in water, or the Selkie plans to swim away. There is no advantage in any Social or Mental situation (unless when in Sea Lion form the Selkie can talk with other Sea Lion, which is a very situational advantage) so it is not a very useful birthright.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T06:40:05-07:00","id":1142120,"title":"","content":"Since the stats are so similar, as a ST I'd just keep attributes and abilities the same in both forms and have the animal form give a bite attack for lethal damage. I'd recommend looking up Sea Lions and Seals on Wikipedia and Youtube to get idea for how they could add to a chronicle. Seals are much better adapted for sea life for example but a Sea Lion is much more dangerous on land. Think of a Sea Lion form like a Kindred's wolf form and a Seal form as like a Rokea's Shark form (particualy larger seal species if your ST allows them). You could also rule that they gain an armour point vs bashing and lethal damage from the thick layer of blubber that seals possess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15685-up-to-eleven","name":"Up-to-Eleven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}